Patch summary:
Android 17 SurfaceFlinger and RenderEngine fixes:
- fc64768935: commit() holds the pacesetter FrameTarget by pointer and reloads
  it after display transactions and mode changes, which can destroy it (a
  use-after-free on a hotplug reconnect or a resolution change).
- 5b950c67dc: a commit retries after propagating a hotplug disconnect when any
  display in it is gone, not only the pacesetter, and regardless of
  pacesetter_selection.
- ddba2662d5: demotePacesetterDisplay checks the pacesetter ID before use.
- d8bf49da92 (without its flag): RenderEngine skips waiting on a fence that has
  already signaled, which saves a driver fence and a host round trip on a
  virtual GPU.
- b5ee9e8ab6: RenderEngine enables only the Vulkan extensions and features it
  uses (Venus and guest_lavapipe run it on Vulkan).

